concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-1-sec-2-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 Exempt citizenship documents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-2-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Section 11 does not apply to a document required or permitted to be produced in connection with:  (a) ascertaining whether a person is, or remains, an Australian citizen; or  (b) the operation of a provision of a citizenship law that relates to:  (i) registration; or  (ii) an application for, or the giving of, an approval to become an Australian citizen; or  (iii) an application for, or the giving of, a notice about evidence of Australian citizenship; or  (iv) the cancellation or surrender of a notice about evidence of Australian citizenship; or  (v) the renunciation of Australian citizenship; or  (vi) the revocation of Australian citizenship; or  (c) the operation of a provision of a citizenship law that relates to:  (i) the keeping of a register; or  (ii) the correction of an entry in a register; or  (iii) the cancellation of an entry in a register.  (2) In this clause: citizenship law means:  (a) the Australian Citizenship Act 2007; or  (b) regulations under that Act. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383  Schedule 1  Consequential amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Section 11 does not apply to a document required or permitted to be produced in connection with:  (a) ascertaining whether a person is, or remains, an Australian citizen; or  (b) the operation of a provision of a citizenship law that relates to:  (i) registration; or  (ii) an application for, or the giving of, an approval to become an Australian citizen; or  (iii) an application for, or the giving of, a notice about evidence of Australian citizenship; or  (iv) the cancellation or surrender of a notice about evidence of Australian citizenship; or  (v) the renunciation of Australian citizenship; or  (vi) the revocation of Australian citizenship; or  (c) the operation of a provision of a citizenship law that relates to:  (i) the keeping of a register; or  (ii) the correction of an entry in a register; or  (iii) the cancellation of an entry in a register.  (2) In this clause: citizenship law means:  (a) the Australian Citizenship Act 2007; or  (b) regulations under that Act. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383  Schedule 1  Consequential amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ab8a56214a226d3f5ca2dd2c457904bc9b95500f0db1845af730aed0140bc3e4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-1-sec-2-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-1-sec-2-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf, p.11" .
